## Why This Is Asked

Tests reasoning with Kleene 3-valued logic on implications and disjunctions, plus a concrete backtracking strategy that preserves non-F constraints while allowing Unknowns.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued semantics
- Implication as ¬A ∨ B
- Propagation and pruning in backtracking
- Constructing a concrete satisfying assignment with U

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal 3-valued logic helpers
const order = {F:0, U:1, T:2};
function not(v){ return v==='T'?'F':v==='F'?'T':'U';}
function or(a,b){ return order[a] >= order[b] ? a : b; }
function and(a,b){ return order[a] <= order[b] ? a : b; }
function implies(a,b){ return or(not(a), b); }
```

